    "answer": {
      "short": "The base is $7\\text{ cm}$ and the perpendicular height is $5\\text{ cm}$. The $6\\text{ cm}$ sloping side is not used in the area formula.",
      "worked": "$$A=\\frac{bh}{2}$$\nThe formula uses only the base and perpendicular height. Here $b=7\\text{ cm}$ and $h=5\\text{ cm}$, so Jimmy should use $\\frac{1}{2}\\times7\\times5$. His extra factor of $6$ incorrectly includes the sloping side.",
